WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.865 --> 00:00:17.957
Brooklyn arrived early for practice on Monday after school.

2
00:00:20.819 --> 00:00:24.902
Before she pushed through the gym door, she heard a ball bouncing on the court.

3
00:00:28.285 --> 00:00:33.020
Inside she saw just one player—Marv.

4
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:37.102
The coach was dribbling a big brown ball instead of the usual orange one.

5
00:00:37.883 --> 00:00:40.664
He circled around and dribbled the ball between his legs.

6
00:00:44.026 --> 00:00:47.108
Then he threw it behind his head without looking at the basket.

7
00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:51.330
Swoosh! Brooklyn clapped.

8
00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:54.412
"Great shot!

9
00:00:54.832 --> 00:00:56.313
What's with that old-school ball?"

10
00:00:56.333 --> 00:01:00.395
"When I played college hoops, we used this type of ball."

11
00:01:01.395 --> 00:01:02.096
Marv laughed.

12
00:01:03.168 --> 00:01:06.531
"Dribbling this thing is like dribbling a watermelon, but it's fun.

13
00:01:07.192 --> 00:01:08.593
Ready to set up for practice?"

14
00:01:08.613 --> 00:01:11.595
"Sure," said Brooklyn.

15
00:01:11.615 --> 00:01:12.937
"How's Coach?"

16
00:01:13.617 --> 00:01:16.059
"He's home from the hospital and trying to rest.

17
00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:19.082
But it won't be easy once the babies come home."

18
00:01:20.023 --> 00:01:23.806
Coach and his wife had their triplets now: two girls and one boy.

19
00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:27.389
Poor Coach had to rest for a few weeks on pillows.

20
00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:30.292
It wasn't his hip that had been injured.

21
00:01:31.248 --> 00:01:35.952
"I can't coach with a broken rear end," he'd told the team when they'd visited him at the

22
00:01:36.012 --> 00:01:38.574
hospital. "Marv will be in charge.

23
00:01:38.854 --> 00:01:40.075
Brooklyn will assist him."

24
00:01:40.956 --> 00:01:43.458
Brooklyn pulled a large binder from her backpack.

25
00:01:43.478 --> 00:01:48.202
"Marv, wait until you see these plays I collected!"

26
00:01:48.222 --> 00:01:51.905
"Let's wait until after warm-ups, Brooklyn."

27
00:01:51.925 --> 00:01:57.249
"But—" time!"

28
00:01:57.769 --> 00:02:00.832
Jacey cried, entering the gym with some other Whales.

29
00:02:01.672 --> 00:02:02.473
"Fun time!"

30
00:02:02.913 --> 00:02:04.274
several players echoed.

31
00:02:04.294 --> 00:02:05.755
"Team time!

32
00:02:06.035 --> 00:02:06.655
Fun time!"

33
00:02:07.076 --> 00:02:09.277
was one of Coach Teagan's favorite sayings.

34
00:02:09.898 --> 00:02:14.421
He told the Whales to forget about friends and problems and everything else during practice.

35
00:02:14.441 --> 00:02:20.385
"Team time" meant it was time to do one thing: play basketball.

36
00:02:21.445 --> 00:02:25.268
Brooklyn opened the equipment bag and twenty basketballs rolled out.

37
00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:31.452
Then she scanned the court, taking attendance.

38
00:02:32.208 --> 00:02:34.769
Every Whales player, except Dirk, was on the court.

39
00:02:35.549 --> 00:02:41.151
She knew Dirk was mad about the big bruises under his eyes and Brooklyn's new job as assistant

40
00:02:41.211 --> 00:02:44.673
coach. But that didn't mean he could skip practice.

41
00:02:44.693 --> 00:02:49.114
"Maybe Marv excused him," Brooklyn thought.

42
00:02:49.795 --> 00:02:53.376
During warm-ups Brooklyn tossed back balls that bounced off the court.

43
00:03:00.332 --> 00:03:03.955
She also took notes whenever she thought of anything that might help the team.

44
00:03:06.296 --> 00:03:10.339
As soon as Marv blew the whistle for a break, Brooklyn ran over to him.

45
00:03:14.262 --> 00:03:15.642
noticed a bunch of problems!"

46
00:03:16.003 --> 00:03:16.743
she burst out.

47
00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:19.465
"Stuart and Aaron are traveling with the ball.

48
00:03:20.065 --> 00:03:21.927
Jacey needs to tighten up her dribbling."

49
00:03:21.947 --> 00:03:25.689
"We'll work on those things," Marv murmured.

50
00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:27.390
He looked around the gym.

51
00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.452
"Dirk still isn't here?"

52
00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:31.501
Brooklyn shook her head.

53
00:03:31.521 --> 00:03:34.542
"I thought maybe you'd excused him from practice."

54
00:03:34.562 --> 00:03:38.404
"Nope. Please call him and report back to me."

55
00:03:40.145 --> 00:03:42.967
Brooklyn found Dirk's cell phone number and dialed it.

56
00:03:46.008 --> 00:03:48.850
"No answer," she told Marv a few minutes later.

57
00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.611
"I left a message for him."

58
00:03:51.591 --> 00:03:52.432
Marv sighed.

59
00:03:54.373 --> 00:03:56.834
"We need Dirk in practice to work on our plays.

60
00:03:57.394 --> 00:04:00.136
I'll see if Coach has a home number for him in the office."

61
00:04:01.184 --> 00:04:02.345
He blew the whistle again.

62
00:04:02.365 --> 00:04:05.427
"Take two more minutes, team."

63
00:04:07.688 --> 00:04:11.710
Brooklyn wrote down some more notes as Jacey jogged past to get her water bottle.

64
00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:15.653
"Hey, Brooklyn, are you doing homework?"

65
00:04:16.113 --> 00:04:16.833
Jacey called.

66
00:04:16.853 --> 00:04:20.495
"No, I'm keeping practice notes," Brooklyn answered.

67
00:04:20.515 --> 00:04:22.897
"I've already noticed some problems."

68
00:04:24.137 --> 00:04:25.538
She reached for Jacey's ball.

69
00:04:25.558 --> 00:04:28.692
"I have a tip for you, Jacey.

70
00:04:28.712 --> 00:04:31.434
You need to dribble closer to your body to protect the ball."

71
00:04:32.875 --> 00:04:35.477
Stuart dashed over and grabbed the ball from Brooklyn.

72
00:04:35.497 --> 00:04:39.680
"Stuart steals!"

73
00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:42.162
He ran to a net and scored.

74
00:04:45.964 --> 00:04:46.845
Brooklyn smiled.

75
00:04:46.865 --> 00:04:52.449
"Well, that illustrates my point: tighten up your dribbling or the ball will get stolen from you."

76
00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:54.190
Jacey frowned.

77
00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:56.372
"You're not our coach, Brooklyn."

78
00:04:57.428 --> 00:04:59.389
Just then the gym door swung open.

79
00:05:00.849 --> 00:05:02.990
Dirk entered and put down his gym bag.

80
00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:06.952
"Let's play ball!"

81
00:05:06.972 --> 00:05:09.513
"You're late," Brooklyn said.

82
00:05:09.533 --> 00:05:11.694
"Take three laps around the court.

83
00:05:12.134 --> 00:05:14.035
Remember Coach's rules for tardiness."

84
00:05:14.055 --> 00:05:16.536
"But Coach isn't here, is he?"

85
00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:19.857
Dirk pretended to look for him under his gym bag.

86
00:05:19.877 --> 00:05:24.279
"Coach?" Jacey laughed loudly.

87
00:05:24.299 --> 00:05:26.380
"Good one!"

88
00:05:27.724 --> 00:05:28.965
Brooklyn crossed her arms.

89
00:05:28.985 --> 00:05:31.026
"You know the rules, Dirk."

90
00:05:32.167 --> 00:05:33.849
Marv returned from the gym office.

91
00:05:33.869 --> 00:05:37.211
"I'll handle this, Brooklyn.

92
00:05:37.771 --> 00:05:39.052
Dirk, let's chat."

93
00:05:39.933 --> 00:05:42.255
Some other Whales began throwing passes.

94
00:05:47.678 --> 00:05:50.340
Brooklyn watched Marv nod as he listened to Dirk.

95
00:05:51.341 --> 00:05:55.164
A few minutes later, Dirk ran onto the court and grabbed a basketball.

96
00:05:58.092 --> 00:06:02.294
He tossed several long shots, swooshing the ball through the hoop each time.

97
00:06:09.077 --> 00:06:10.617
copy Dirk," Marv said.

98
00:06:10.637 --> 00:06:11.858
"Free throws.

99
00:06:12.158 --> 00:06:13.338
Do at least twenty each."

100
00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:20.301
While the Whales practiced, Brooklyn pulled some pages from her binder.

101
00:06:22.662 --> 00:06:29.649
The pages showed step-by-step instructions for Hip-Hop Delight, a play executed last year by the women's team at

102
00:06:29.689 --> 00:06:31.189
the University of Connecticut.

103
00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:34.150
It had won them a championship game.

104
00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:38.291
Brooklyn had numbered and sketched each step in the play.

105
00:06:40.412 --> 00:06:42.372
She pointed at one of the sketches for Marv.

106
00:06:42.392 --> 00:06:45.293
"Can we try this with our team?"

107
00:06:46.454 --> 00:06:48.314
Marv studied the play for a few minutes.

108
00:06:48.334 --> 00:06:50.375
"You think like a coach, kid!

109
00:06:50.855 --> 00:06:53.996
This Hip-Hop Delight play will definitely confuse opponents.

110
00:06:54.376 --> 00:06:55.076
Let's try it!"

111
00:06:56.064 --> 00:06:58.465
The two coaches joined the players under a net.

112
00:07:00.765 --> 00:07:03.886
Marv instructed each player where to stand to start the play.

113
00:07:04.466 --> 00:07:05.907
He gave a basketball to Dirk.

114
00:07:05.927 --> 00:07:10.348
"Toss the ball away from our net first, across your left hip.

115
00:07:10.728 --> 00:07:11.588
Pass it to Aaron.

116
00:07:12.469 --> 00:07:16.210
He'll dribble to midcourt to Jacey, passing the ball to her right side.

117
00:07:17.230 --> 00:07:22.231
This is a complicated play," Marv added, "but if it works, we'll score points.

118
00:07:22.571 --> 00:07:23.192
Right, Brooklyn?"

119
00:07:23.212 --> 00:07:26.857
"Right!" Marv blew his whistle.

120
00:07:28.478 --> 00:07:29.059
"Let's go!"

121
00:07:29.839 --> 00:07:30.620
Dirk dribbled.

122
00:07:33.222 --> 00:07:38.666
He turned, throwing the ball to Aaron, but Marv quickly blew his whistle again to stop practice.

123
00:07:38.686 --> 00:07:43.110
"Dirk, go the other way before passing the ball."

124
00:07:44.231 --> 00:07:47.073
After five tries Dirk stomped over to Marv.

125
00:07:47.093 --> 00:07:50.996
"This play makes no sense!"

126
00:07:51.016 --> 00:07:53.698
"Calm down," said Marv.

127
00:07:53.718 --> 00:07:55.460
"This is a smart play.

128
00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.621
With practice, we can make it work.

129
00:07:58.121 --> 00:07:59.501
Brooklyn, show him your sketch."

130
00:08:00.482 --> 00:08:01.922
Dirk's face turned red.

131
00:08:01.942 --> 00:08:04.023
"She planned this play?

132
00:08:04.503 --> 00:08:05.904
No wonder it doesn't work!"

133
00:08:07.064 --> 00:08:08.525
Brooklyn held up her sketches.

134
00:08:08.545 --> 00:08:14.848
"All you have to do—" "Girls can't coach guys, especially not you!"

135
00:08:15.408 --> 00:08:16.888
Dirk stormed out of the gym.

136
00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:20.910
Marv called after him.

137
00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:22.331
"Dirk! Stop!"

138
00:08:22.351 --> 00:08:27.256
"I know this play can work," Brooklyn said, looking at the rest of the team.

139
00:08:28.257 --> 00:08:29.937
Jacey frowned and shook her head.

140
00:08:30.557 --> 00:08:32.198
The other players were looking away.

141
00:08:32.218 --> 00:08:36.959
"Dirk will start Thursday's game on the bench," Marv announced.

142
00:08:36.979 --> 00:08:40.760
"Great," Jacey muttered sarcastically.

143
00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:44.561
"Will your big play work without our best player, Brooklyn?"

144
00:08:44.581 --> 00:08:48.203
"Enough!" Marv pointed sharply at Jacey.

145
00:08:48.223 --> 00:08:51.043
"You just earned a spot on the bench too!"

146
00:08:51.944 --> 00:08:53.004
Brooklyn looked down.

147
00:08:53.672 --> 00:08:58.456
"It always takes time for players to accept a new coach," she told herself.

148
00:08:59.477 --> 00:09:02.819
She just hoped it would happen before play-offs began.
